# Dual-Backend AI Architecture (Groq & Local LLM) with LangChain, LangGraph, and LangSmith

Extend the SnowWiki ServiceNow assistant with a modular, industry-standard architecture that supports both cloud inference via **Groq** and a self-hosted local model via **FastAPI** (OpenAI-compatible `/v1/chat/completions` over HTTPS). Orchestration is structured using **LangChain**, **LangGraph**, and **LangSmith**.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Environment Toggle**: A single boolean `USE_LOCAL_LLM` (true/false) controls whether requests route to Groq or the local FastAPI endpoint.
> - **Model Variables**: `SMALL_MODEL_NAME` (classifier/intent) and `LARGE_MODEL_NAME` (RAG/response) are defined as environment variables, initially defaulting to `"test-model"`.
> - **Authentication**: No API key is required for the local FastAPI server. Client-side requests will set `verify=False` to support self-signed SSL certificates.
> - **Backward Compatibility**: Existing retrieval, ChromaDB vector indexing, and fallback search functionality remain intact and are orchestrated by the LangGraph pipeline.

