### 2. Local LLM Server (FastAPI)

#### [NEW] [local_llm_server.py](file:///d:/SnowWiki/local_llm_server.py)
- Implement lightweight FastAPI application exposing `POST /v1/chat/completions`.
- OpenAI-compatible request and response schemas using Pydantic (`ChatRequest`, `Message`, `choices`, `usage`).
- Pluggable `_call_underlying_llm(model, prompt)` stub returning `f"[{model}] Echo: {prompt}"` for immediate testing on laptop and deployment on the target company server.

---

### 3. LLM Adapters & Chains (LangChain)

#### [NEW] [src/llm_wrapper.py](file:///d:/SnowWiki/src/llm_wrapper.py)
- `GroqLLM(LLM)`: LangChain LLM wrapper invoking `groq.Groq().chat.completions.create`.
- `LocalLLM(LLM)`: LangChain LLM wrapper posting JSON to `{LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT}/v1/chat/completions` (with SSL verify disabled for self-signed certificates).
- `get_llm(kind: str = "classifier") -> LLM`: Factory returning `LocalLLM` or `GroqLLM` based on `USE_LOCAL_LLM` and selecting `SMALL_MODEL_NAME` vs `LARGE_MODEL_NAME` (or Groq models).

#### [NEW] [src/chains.py](file:///d:/SnowWiki/src/chains.py)
- `INTENT_SYSTEM_PROMPT`: PromptTemplate for ServiceNow intent classification (`GREETING | SERVICENOW | OUT_OF_SCOPE`).
- `RAG_ANSWER_PROMPT`: PromptTemplate for grounded ServiceNow technical answering with memory and retrieved chunks.
- Helper functions `intent_classification_chain()` and `rag_answer_chain()`.

